WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.339
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:09.071
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.371 --> 00:00:15.692
Unit three: Comparatives & Superlatives. Today you will compare two things and say which is the best.

4
00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:18.784
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:22.931
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:24.494
Bigger.

7
00:00:25.483 --> 00:00:27.297
Bigger means larger than something.

8
00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:29.790
An elephant is bigger than a cow.

9
00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:32.536
Your turn. Say: Bigger.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.088
Bigger.

11
00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:37.851
Biggest.

12
00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.117
Biggest means larger than all others.

13
00:00:41.717 --> 00:00:43.194
It is the biggest city.

14
00:00:43.783 --> 00:00:45.971
Your turn. Say: Biggest.

15
00:00:48.833 --> 00:00:49.788
Biggest.

16
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.470
Faster.

17
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:54.413
Faster means quicker than something.

18
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:57.028
A train is faster than a bus.

19
00:00:57.617 --> 00:00:59.793
Your turn. Say: Faster.

20
00:01:02.633 --> 00:01:03.495
Faster.

21
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.356
Fastest.

22
00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:08.698
Fastest means quicker than all others.

23
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:11.422
A cheetah is the fastest animal.

24
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.402
Your turn. Say: Fastest.

25
00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.279
Fastest.

26
00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:20.262
More beautiful.

27
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:24.225
More beautiful means nicer to look at than something.

28
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.188
This temple is more beautiful than that one.

29
00:01:27.783 --> 00:01:30.645
Your turn. Say: More beautiful.

30
00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.722
More beautiful.

31
00:01:35.483 --> 00:01:36.624
Most beautiful.

32
00:01:37.617 --> 00:01:40.011
Most beautiful means nicest to look at of all.

33
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:42.547
It is the most beautiful place.

34
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.452
Your turn. Say: Most beautiful.

35
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.557
Most beautiful.

36
00:01:51.317 --> 00:01:51.900
Than.

37
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:55.603
Than means the word for the second part of a comparison.

38
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.566
He is taller than me.

39
00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.605
Your turn. Say: Than.

40
00:02:03.467 --> 00:02:03.992
Than.

41
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:05.705
Compare.

42
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:09.529
Compare means to look at how things are alike or different.

43
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:11.710
Compare the two prices.

44
00:02:12.317 --> 00:02:14.772
Your turn. Say: Compare.

45
00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:18.692
Compare.

46
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:23.081
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.917 --> 00:02:27.974
Visal, who is taller, you or your brother? Use a comparative.

48
00:02:29.083 --> 00:02:38.623
My brother is taller than me. A comparative compares two things. For short adjectives we add -er and than: tall, taller than.

49
00:02:39.717 --> 00:02:41.124
And the superlative?

50
00:02:42.217 --> 00:02:53.614
It compares three or more things. We use the + -est: the tallest. For long adjectives we use more and the most: more beautiful, the most beautiful.

51
00:02:54.717 --> 00:02:56.426
Are there irregular forms?

52
00:02:57.517 --> 00:03:10.881
Yes. Good, better, the best. Bad, worse, the worst. Far, further, the furthest. Also remember spelling: big, bigger, the biggest; happy, happier, the happiest.

53
00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:13.394
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.608
Grammar focus: Comparatives and superlatives.

55
00:03:17.908 --> 00:03:19.025
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:21.449
My brother is taller than me.

57
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.814
This temple is more beautiful than that one.

58
00:03:25.717 --> 00:03:28.343
A cheetah is the fastest animal in the world.

59
00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:39.780
Comparative: adjective + -er + than, or more + adjective + than. Superlative: the + -est, or the most + adjective. Learn better / worse and best / worst.

60
00:03:40.517 --> 00:03:43.715
Be careful! Don't say: She is more tall than me.

61
00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.956
Say: She is taller than me.

62
00:03:48.256 --> 00:03:50.558
Use -er with short adjectives.

63
00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:53.775
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.661
Which Is Better?.

65
00:03:55.961 --> 00:03:58.947
A car is faster than a bike, but a bike is healthier.

66
00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:03.721
Phnom Penh is bigger than my town, and it is the biggest city in the country.

67
00:04:04.733 --> 00:04:07.418
I think Angkor Wat is the most beautiful temple.

68
00:04:08.433 --> 00:04:12.499
My English is better than last year, but it is not the best in the class.

69
00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:15.546
We use than to compare two things.

70
00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:20.414
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.180
A giraffe is blank than a horse.

72
00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.110
A, tall. B, taller. C, tallest.

73
00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:32.910
The answer is B: taller.

74
00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.887
This is the blank beautiful park.

75
00:04:36.187 --> 00:04:39.353
A, most. B, more. C, much.

76
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.551
The answer is A: most.

77
00:04:45.717 --> 00:04:47.905
He plays blank than me. (good)

78
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:51.208
A, gooder. B, better. C, best.

79
00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.859
The answer is B: better.

80
00:04:58.017 --> 00:04:59.703
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:00.003 --> 00:05:06.117
A, She is more tall than me.. B, She is taller than me.. C, She is tallest than me..

82
00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:12.467
The answer is B: She is taller than me..

83
00:05:13.617 --> 00:05:16.115
According to the reading, which city is the biggest?

84
00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:20.185
A, Phnom Penh. B, my town. C, Siem Reap.

85
00:05:23.733 --> 00:05:26.070
The answer is A: Phnom Penh.

86
00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.453
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:31.317 --> 00:05:34.489
Compare two things you own using a comparative form.

88
00:05:43.283 --> 00:05:44.644
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:58.803
My phone is newer than my laptop, but my laptop is more useful for studying. I use newer and more useful to compare them. I add -er to short adjectives and more before long adjectives.

90
00:05:59.103 --> 00:06:00.743
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:06.264
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and comparatives and superlatives.

92
00:06:06.564 --> 00:06:11.411
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

93
00:06:11.711 --> 00:06:14.178
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

94
00:06:14.478 --> 00:06:17.316
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

